issue_context.body:
### Tested versions

- Reproducible in Godot (mono) v4.2.1

### System information

Arch Linux

### Issue description

Setting font properties via SetCustomFont() and SetCustomFontSize() of a TreeItem don’t actually redraw the TreeItem, making it impossible to change the TreeItem’s font and fontsize on the fly. The visual representation of an item only seems to update when changing its text or rebuilding the tree.

A somewhat gentle workaround for now is to reset the item text while adding whitespace (just resetting the same text is ignored).

### Steps to reproduce

Add this script to a Tree node:

```C#
public partial class tree : Tree
{
	public override void _Ready()
	{
		CreateItem();
		TreeItem treeItem = CreateItem();
		treeItem.SetText(0, "Clicking me should change my font size");

		ItemSelected += _OnItemSelected;
	}

	public void _OnItemSelected()
	{
		TreeItem treeItem = GetSelected();
		treeItem.SetCustomFontSize(0, 20);
		//treeItem.SetText(0, "I'm now 20px"); <-- Uncommenting this line needed to update item
	}
}```

The item is only updated once the last line is uncommented.

